  "title": "NVIDIA built a sandbox for AI agents",
  "narration": "NVIDIA just built a seatbelt for AI agents. OpenShell is an open-source runtime that puts agents like Claude Code and Codex inside policy-controlled sandboxes, so they can write files, call APIs and use credentials without getting the keys to everything. The clever bit is enforcement happens outside the agent: kernel rules gate files and system calls, network requests are checked against policy, and credentials are injected only for approved destinations. NVIDIA also pairs it with Sentry, a BlueField watchdog that can quarantine agents in milliseconds. Catch: OpenShell is still 0.1.x. But autonomous agents finally have something resembling adult supervision.",
